║   Mesh ML-spike   vllm 0.20.1 · transformers 5.7.0 · py 3.11.15    ║
╠══ Round-7.6 V18 pipeline (run from project root) ══════════════════╣
║                                                                    ║
║  1. Start Music Flamingo (terminal A)                              ║
║       bash spike/track-grading/serve_music_flamingo.sh   # :8001   ║
║                                                                    ║
║  2. Caption sweep (terminal B in devshell)             ~7 hr       ║
║       bash spike/track-grading/run_round7_6_pipeline.sh caption-full
║                                                                    ║
║  3. Text-LLM rating — N independent jurors. Each tag writes its own║
║     NPZ; step 5 (v18-train) auto-aggregates them via Dawid-Skene.  ║
║                                                                    ║
║  ★ START 3A + 3B AS SOON AS STEP 1 IS UP — they run on REMOTE GPUs ║
║    (Spark 1, Spark 2), so they share nothing with caption-full and ║
║    overlap fully with step 2. The streaming runner polls the       ║
║    captions dir every 5 min and exits ~20 min after step 2 ends.   ║
║                                                                    ║
║     3A) Spark 2 / Nemotron-30B (terminal C, parallel with step 2)  ║
║       export TEXT_LLM_URL=http://172.16.54.147:8000/v1/chat/completions
║       export TEXT_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B-NVFP4
║       export TEXT_LLM_TAG=nemotron  TEXT_LLM_NO_THINK=1            ║
║       ./...pipeline.sh caption-rate-streaming                      ║
║                                                                    ║
║     3B) Spark 1 / Qwen3.6-27B (terminal D, parallel with step 2)   ║
║       export TEXT_LLM_URL=http://172.16.51.90:8000/v1/chat/completions
║       export TEXT_LLM_MODEL=sakamakismile/Qwen3.6-27B-Text-NVFP4-MTP
║       export TEXT_LLM_TAG=qwen36  TEXT_LLM_NO_THINK=1  TEXT_LLM_WORKERS=16
║       ./...pipeline.sh caption-rate-streaming                      ║
║                                                                    ║
║     3C) Local Mistral-Small-3.2-24B AWQ — SEQUENTIAL, after step 2:║
║       pkill -f 'python.*api_server'         # frees GPU from MF    ║
║       TEXT_LLM_MODEL=gghfez/Mistral-Small-3.2-24B-Instruct-hf-AWQ \║
║         bash spike/track-grading/serve_text_llm.sh   # :8002       ║
║       TEXT_LLM_TAG=local_mistral \                                 ║
║         bash ...pipeline.sh caption-rate                           ║
║     (Devstral-Small-2507 ships bf16-only ~48 GB → won't fit 24 GB  ║
║      5090. Mistral-Small-3.2 is Devstral's pre-code-fine-tune base.║
║      For natural-language intensity rating the base is fine —      ║
║      arguably better-calibrated than the code-tuned variant.)      ║
║                                                                    ║
║     Tail-latency tweak: STABLE_SECS=300 POLL_SECS=60 ./...streaming║
║                                                                    ║
║  4. Free GPU before teacher training                               ║
║       pkill -f 'python.*api_server'                                ║
║                                                                    ║
║  5. Train V18 (consensus→teacher→student→eval→export) ~2 hr        ║
║       bash spike/track-grading/run_round7_6_pipeline.sh v18-train  ║
║                                                                    ║
║  6. Inspect                                                        ║
║       less <mesh-track-grading>/round7_6_eval_report.md            ║
║       ls   models/aggression-axes/V18_round7_6_*.json              ║
║                                                                    ║
